  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of safe drinking water</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CMWU, will provide necessary water materials and fittings to carry out repair works on water networks in Gaza City. CMWU will engage local contractors for digging filling, transportation and labour for the repairs of pipes and fitting. CMWU will receive pipes andfittings from ICRC and UNICEF as in-kind donation whereas installation and rehabilitation cost will be supported under this project. Oxfam will provide technical guidance and support to CMWU field engineers to reinforce quality and gender responsiveness.  Primarily focused on Al Jalaa Street, the proposed repair works will connect the main 14-inch water pipeline with its branches (130ML), augmenting the discharge of Mekorot water to the western part of Gaza City, benefitting 30,900 individuals, including IDPs and host communities.

Over the course of a six-month period, the primary aim of this water-focused initiative is to ensure access to safe drinking water for 36,050 vulnerable individuals, including IDPs and host communities, thereby reducing the risks of dehydration and waterborne diseases in Gaza City. Oxfam and its partner will pursue this objective through a two-pronged approach, involving immediate relief via water trucking and the repair of the 14-inch pipeline branches (130ML), to increase the discharge of Mekorot water  (watersupply company) to the western part of Gaza City, catering to the needs of the 30,900 individuals, including IDPs and host communities in the Al Jalaa area.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal Municipalities Water Utilit</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Coastal Municipal Water Utility (CMWU) is an autonomous regional water and wastewater utility that provides drinking water supply and wastewater collection and treatment services within their jurisdiction (Rafah area). It is responsible for the construction, operation and maintenance of water extraction and distribution systems; treatment of water sources up to the standards set by PWA; construction, operation and maintenance of sewage infrastructure; and treatment of wastewater up to the standards set by the PWA. CMWU will provide the technical support for the design and rehabilitation supervision of the implementation of desalination plants in addition work with Oxfam and PEF in the community public awareness as well as the water monitoring system.
Oxfam#s partner, CMWU, hasextensive experience in water, desalination and wastewater services, and has implemented projects funded by the European Union and other international agencies in the construction and rehabilitation of desalination plants. Building on this collective experience, the intervention will be the first in Gaza#s unique context with full support of the local government to strictly monitor the water quality of desalinated water in the Gaza strip</narrative>
  </participating-org>
